#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:3
msgid "Manage installed apps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:5
msgid ""
"List, upgrade, and remove the apps pipx manages, then confirm each change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:9
msgid "List apps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:11
#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:99
#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:145
msgid "$ pipx list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:15
msgid ""
"The output shows each package version, its apps, and the environment paths. "
"Narrow or reshape it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:17
msgid "``pipx list --short`` prints package names and versions only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:18
msgid ""
"``pipx list --include-injected`` also lists packages injected into each "
"environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:19
msgid "``pipx list --outdated`` lists environments with an available upgrade."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:20
msgid "``pipx list --pinned`` lists pinned environments only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:24
msgid "Upgrade one"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:26
msgid "$ pipx upgrade black"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:30
msgid ""
"Add ``--include-injected`` to upgrade injected packages alongside the main "
"app. Pass ``--install`` to install the package spec when it is missing "
"rather than error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:33
msgid ""
"pipx exposes any apps, manual pages, and shell completions the new version "
"adds, and removes the ones it no longer ships, so ``pipx list`` and "
"``PIPX_BIN_DIR`` match the upgraded package. ``upgrade-all`` and ``pipx "
"install --upgrade`` do the same."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:37
#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:65
#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:81
#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:97
#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:117
#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:143
msgid "Verify:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:39
#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:83
#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:119
msgid "$ pipx list --short"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:45
msgid "Upgrade all"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:47
msgid "$ pipx upgrade-all"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:51
msgid ""
"Use ``--skip PKG ...`` to leave named environments untouched, and ``--"
"include-injected`` to include injected packages. Pinned environments are "
"skipped; see :doc:`pin-packages`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:54
msgid ""
"pipx upgrades up to eight environments at once and prints their output in "
"environment order, as a one-at-a-time run would. An app, manual page, or "
"completion that several environments expose ends up with the same "
"environment as in a one-at-a-time run. A failed environment does not stop "
"the others. pip and uv cannot prompt for input, such as index credentials, "
"during any pipx command other than ``pipx runpip``. Pass ``--verbose`` to "
"upgrade them one at a time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:59
msgid ""
"Ctrl-C, ``SIGTERM`` or ``SIGHUP`` stops pipx from starting more upgrades, "
"and pipx finishes the ones already in progress before it exits, since an "
"upgrade cut short leaves an environment with a mix of old and new files. "
"Press Ctrl-C again to stop those too. pipx then reports each environment it "
"stopped mid-upgrade, ``pipx list`` flags it, and the next ``pipx upgrade-"
"all``, ``pipx upgrade`` or ``pipx reinstall`` of it reinstalls it from its "
"metadata. With ``--verbose`` the first Ctrl-C already stops the running "
"upgrade."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:67
msgid "$ pipx list --outdated"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:73
msgid "Uninstall one"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:75
msgid "$ pipx uninstall black"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:79
msgid ""
"pipx deletes the environment and unlinks its apps, manual pages, and shell "
"completions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:89
msgid "Uninstall all"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:91
msgid "$ pipx uninstall-all"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:95
msgid ""
"Record what you have first with ``pipx list --short`` if you plan to "
"reinstall later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:105
msgid "Reinstall one"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:107
msgid ""
"Rebuild an environment from its recorded metadata, keeping the same options "
"as the original install. Reach for it after a Python upgrade or to repair a "
"broken environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:110
msgid "$ pipx reinstall black"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:114
msgid ""
"Pass ``--python`` to rebuild under another interpreter. ``pipx install --"
"force`` keeps the environment's interpreter and ignores ``--python``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:125
msgid "Reinstall all"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:127
msgid "$ pipx reinstall-all"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:131
msgid ""
"Common after installing a new Python version so every app moves to it. Use "
"``--python`` to target a specific interpreter and ``--skip PKG ...`` to "
"exclude environments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:134
msgid ""
"pipx rebuilds up to eight environments at once (fewer on machines with fewer "
"CPUs) and holds back the output of each until the ones before it finish, so "
"it reads the same as a one-at-a-time run. An app, manual page, or completion "
"that several environments expose ends up with the same environment as in a "
"one-at-a-time run. A failed environment does not stop the others. pip and uv "
"cannot prompt for input, such as index credentials, during any pipx command "
"other than ``pipx runpip``. Pass ``--verbose`` to rebuild them one at a time "
"and watch the pip or uv output as it happens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:140
msgid ""
"Ctrl-C, ``SIGTERM`` or ``SIGHUP`` stops the rebuilds in progress and "
"restores each of those environments from its backup; the environments "
"already rebuilt keep their new build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/manage-installed-apps.rst:151
msgid ""
"To check environments without changing them, or to repair only the broken "
"ones, see :ref:`repair-environments`."
msgstr ""
